 **Why per-remote trust triad and not binary allow/deny?** Multi-client consultants need search without write-back. A freelance dev working on Client A in the morning and Client B in the afternoon can't let A's code insights leak into a brain Client B can search. Read-only solves that cleanly.
 
-**Why not bundle brain into rig?** Gbrain is a separate, actively-developed project with its own release cadence, schema migrations, and MCP surface. Bundling would mean rig has to gate brain updates, which slows brain improvements from reaching users. Separate-but-integrated lets each ship on its own cadence.
