-**Why `brain init --non-interactive` via env var and not a flag?** Connection strings contain database passwords. Passing them as argv lands the password in `ps`, shell history, and process listings. Env-var handoff keeps the secret in process memory only. Gbrain supports both `BRAIN_DATABASE_URL` and `DATABASE_URL`; we use the former to avoid collisions with non-brain tooling.
